---
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: used in the template below the frontmatter fence, which Biome does not parse for .astro files
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Privacy — Movie Planner">
  <h1
    class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100"
  >
    Privacy
  </h1>
  <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col gap-4 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
    <p>
      This site is fully static. There's no server-side application code of any
      kind in this repository's build output, and no server this project runs
      ever holds — or even sees, not even in transit — your CalDAV or OMDb
      credentials.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your credentials are stored only in your own browser's storage
      (IndexedDB), on this device, in this browser. They're never sent anywhere
      except straight to the CalDAV and OMDb URLs you configured yourself.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every CalDAV and OMDb request this site makes goes directly from your
      browser to the servers you pointed it at — there's no proxy, relay, or
      analytics service of any kind in between. Clearing your browser's site
      data for this origin removes everything this site ever stored.
    </p>
    <p>
      Two features call other services directly, without going through this
      site's own servers (it doesn't have any): searching for a venue's address
      while logging or editing a viewing calls
      <a
        href="https://nominatim.org/"
        class="text-indigo-600 underline dark:text-indigo-400"
      >
        Nominatim
      </a>
      , OpenStreetMap's free geocoder — only when you use that search field, never
      automatically. Any map showing a located venue loads map tiles from OpenStreetMap
      directly, which does happen automatically whenever such a map is on screen.
      Neither service ever receives your CalDAV or OMDb credentials — Nominatim sees
      only the address text you type, and the tile provider sees only the map area
      being viewed.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
